{"name":"Velveteen Crush","hex":"#936064","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"velveteen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cotton fabric with a short pile, resembling velvet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velveteen"},{"term":"crush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A violent collision or compression; a crash; destruction; ruin.","Violent pressure, as of a moving crowd."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To press between two hard objects; to squeeze so as to alter the natural shape or integrity, or to force together into a mass.","To reduce to fine particles by pounding or grinding."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Velveteen","blocks":[{"text":"Velveteen is a type of woven fabric with a dense, even, short pile. It has less sheen than velvet because the pile in velveteen is cut from weft threads, while that of velvet is cut from warp threads. Velveteen also has a shorter pile than velvet and is stiffer, with less drape, and is usually made of cotton or a cotton-silk blend."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Morris_Acanthus_Velveteen_1876.jpg/330px-Morris_Acanthus_Velveteen_1876.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velveteen","wikidata":"Q2914295"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"velveteen":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/42/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-velveteen.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/42/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-velveteen.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-velveteen.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/42/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-velveteen.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-velveteen.wav.ogg"}],"crus